### Physical Layer
The Physical Layer deals with the physical connectors, cables, protocols, and the modulation/demodulation of data onto the carrier media. It typically involves low-level infrastructure.

```cpp
class PhysicalLayer {
public:
    // Method to initialize the physical layer
    static void Initialize();
    // Method to send data over the physical media
    bool sendData(const std::vector<uint8_t>& data);
    // Method to receive data from the physical media
    std::vector<uint8_t> receiveData(int size);

private:
    // Private functions or resources
    PhysicalMedia media;
};
```

### Data Link Layer
The Data Link Layer deals with framing, flow control, and error detection. It is crucial for end-to-end data transmission.

```cpp
class DataLinkLayer {
public:
    DataLinkLayer(const PhysicalLayer& phyLayer);
    ~DataLinkLayer();

    // Method to send a frame over the data link layer
    bool sendData(const std::vector<uint8_t>& data);
    // Method to receive a frame from the data link layer
    std::vector<uint8_t> receiveData(int size);
    // Method to set the physical layer reference
    void setPhysicalLayer(const PhysicalLayer& phyLayer);

private:
    PhysicalLayer* phyLayer;
    FrameBuffer frameBuffer;
};
```

### Network Layer
The Network Layer deals with routing and addressing. It is responsible for indicating the best path for data to travel.

```cpp
class NetworkLayer {
public:
    NetworkLayer(const DataLinkLayer& dataLinkLayer);
    ~NetworkLayer();

    // Method to send a packet over the network layer
    bool sendData(const DataLinkLayer& dataLinkLayer);
    // Method to receive a packet from the network layer
    std::vector<uint8_t> receiveData(int size);
    // Method to set the data link layer reference
    void setDataLinkLayer(const DataLinkLayer& dataLinkLayer);

private:
    DataLinkLayer* dataLinkLayer;
    RoutingTable routingTable;
};
```

### Transport Layer
The Transport Layer deals with error correction, congestion control, and ensuring reliable data transfer. It also handles the handshake phase for client-server communication.

```cpp
class TransportLayer {
public:
    TransportLayer(const NetworkLayer& networkLayer);
    ~TransportLayer();

    // Method to send a segment over the transport layer
    bool sendData(const NetworkLayer& networkLayer);
    // Method to receive a segment from the transport layer
    std::vector<uint8_t> receiveData(int size);
    // Method to set the network layer reference
    void setNetworkLayer(const NetworkLayer& networkLayer);

private:
    NetworkLayer* networkLayer;
    TransportSocket transportSocket;
};
```

### Session Layer
The Session Layer manages session setup, management, and teardown. It allows reliable communications between two applications on different machines.

```cpp
class SessionLayer {
public:
    SessionLayer(const TransportLayer& transportLayer);
    ~SessionLayer();

    // Method to send a session request
    bool handleRequest(const TransportLayer& transportLayer);
    // Method to receive a session response
    std::vector<uint8_t> processResponse(const TransportLayer& transportLayer);
    // Method to set the transport layer reference
    void setTransportLayer(const TransportLayer& transportLayer);

private:
    TransportLayer* transportLayer;
    std::vector<uint8_t> sessionBuffer;
};
```

### Presentation Layer
The Presentation Layer deals with data formatting and encryption/decryption. It also manages data compression and decompression.

```cpp
class PresentationLayer {
public:
    PresentationLayer(const SessionLayer& sessionLayer);
    ~PresentationLayer();

    // Method to encode data
    std::vector<uint8_t> encodeData(const SessionLayer& sessionLayer);
    // Method to decode data
    std::vector<uint8_t> decodeData(const SessionLayer& sessionLayer);

private:
    SessionLayer* sessionLayer;
    DataEncoder encoder;
    DataDecoder decoder;
};
```

### Application Layer
The Application Layer is responsible for end-user applications. It interacts directly with the user and handles all necessary communications.

```cpp
class ApplicationLayer {
public:
    ApplicationLayer(const PresentationLayer& presentationLayer);
    ~ApplicationLayer();

    // Method to process a request from a user
    std::vector<uint8_t> processRequest(const PresentationLayer& presentationLayer);
    // Method to send a response back to the user
    void sendResponse(const PresentationLayer& presentationLayer);

private:
    PresentationLayer* presentationLayer;
};
```

